				"⣿⠃⠀⠀⠀",
				29,
				7
			],
			"Message": "chore(submodules): Update all submodules with latest features and dependency updates\n\nThis commit updates all submodules (Air, Cocoon, Common, Echo, Mountain, Rest, Wind) to their latest versions, integrating new features and improvements across the CodeEditorLand ecosystem.\n\nKey updates include:\n- Air: Implemented gRPC service skeleton with authentication, enabling secure remote operations.\n- Cocoon: Added comprehensive architecture documentation and gRPC services for Mountain integration, enhancing extension host capabilities.\n- Mountain: Enhanced IPC system with native integrations and secure ID generation, improving cross-platform communication.\n- Wind: Completed advanced synchronization services with multi-agent coordination, supporting real-time document sync and conflict resolution.\n- Common, Echo, Rest: Updated dependencies to latest versions for bug fixes and enhancements.\n\nThese updates strengthen the infrastructure, security, and functionality of the ecosystem, advancing towards production-ready standards.",
			"SHA": "c3ed1ab465f31479c0413c2d5994f1abb83c5153"
		},
		{
			"Author": "Nikola Hristov",
			"Date": "2026-01-28T06:38:22Z",
			"File": [
				"⠇⠀⠀⠀⠀",
				29,
				2
			],
			"Message": "chore(submodules): Update Cocoon and Wind submodules with configuration and conflict resolution services\n\nThis commit updates the Cocoon and Wind submodules to their latest versions, introducing new services that enhance the CodeEditorLand ecosystem.\n\n**Cocoon Updates:**\n- Implemented ConfigurationService for the extension host, following VSCode's IConfigurationService interface, to manage settings across APPLICATION, WORKSPACE, and PROFILE scopes.\n- Integrated with Mountain via gRPC for persistent storage and IPC communication, providing a robust foundation for extension configuration management.\n\n**Wind Updates:**\n- Added ConflictResolutionService to handle document conflicts in real-time collaborative editing scenarios, with strategies like 'Accept Local Changes', 'Smart Merge', and auto-resolution for simple conflicts.\n- Enhanced synchronization with conflict severity levels and metrics tracking, improving data consistency and user experience.\n\nThese updates strengthen the configuration management and conflict resolution capabilities, advancing the integration between Wind frontend and Mountain backend systems.",
			"SHA": "8fca0acaf1c761d715fe3293be419f14d094bbea"
		},
